comment_data.body:
This strikes me as a valuable addition to the API, although the concrete proposal is a bit broad. The main question is a general design one: Do we want
1. a full, direct, exposure of the low-level tree-sitter API in Lua;
2. a custom Lua API tuned to our needs (both regarding functionality and API surface);

or both or a mix (the last I would consider not so desirable because harder to reason about and document). 

Extending `iter_children` sounds like a good first step to a useable MVP, although we should keep an eventual refactor on top of a Lua tree cursor API (which has come up in other contexts before).

@neovim/treesitter
